# Interactive Playground

Experiment with `.rocci` templates and `.rocdown` documents live in your browser. All parsing, lowering, AST formatting, and syntax token classification run entirely client-side in WebAssembly.

@docs playground { id: "counter" }

@docs note { title: "About WebAssembly Lowering" }
The playground lowers `.rocci` templates and `.rocdown` documents directly to ordinary Roc source code and S-expression ASTs inside a Web Worker. Rendering generated Roc modules to live HTML requires a Roc runtime in WebAssembly, which is in development.
